    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "** EMAIL ENQUIRIES ONLY ** REFERENCES REQUIRED **\r\n\r\nShauna O'Brien of BROE auctioneers Lettings is thrilled to present this stunning 2/3-bedroom end-of-terrace house available for rent. This property offers generous living space, including an entrance hallway, a lounge (which could be used as a third bedroom), and a bright living room that leads into a kitchen overlooking a spacious garden. Upstairs, you will find two double bedrooms and a family bathroom.The location is second to none in terms of convenience, with an abundance of amenities close at hand in Sundrive, Kimmage, Terenure and Harold’s Cross, including a wide selection of shops, cafés, restaurants, and well-established primary and secondary schools. The new National Children's Hospital is also within easy reach, further enhancing the appeal of this sought-after setting. The area is exceptionally well served by public transport, with numerous bus routes providing swift access to Dublin City Centre, while the extensive road network offers convenient connectivity to the M50 and beyond. \r\n\r\nViewing comes highly recommended by sole letting agents BROE auctioneers.\r\nContact our lettings agent Shauna O’Brien to register your interest today.\r\n\r\nFollow us on Instagram and Facebook at BROE auctioneers to keep up to date with new listings."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: E1"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Viewing Details",
        "SortOrder": 6,
        "Content": "Please note that we give preference to applications via our website https://BROE.ie/ and that enquiries email only, NO PHONE CALLS will be accepted. Due to the high volume of interest, it might not be possible to respond to every application for this advertisement. We're currently experiencing an unprecedented volume of enquiries and we would like to let you know that viewings are available on a limited, first come, first serve basis, and tend to fill up quickly. Apologies for any inconvenience this may cause.\r\n\r\nPlease email your interest and we will be in contact with viewing times."
      }
